{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1136376-cooperation-of-various-splats","id":1136376,"title":"Cooperation of various splats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-01T14:38:49-07:00","id":1136376,"title":"Cooperation of various splats","content":"Yes, I know the Contagion chronicle is going to shed some light on how the various splats might benefit from interacting with each other etc.<br /> However, in light of all the Vs.-threads coming up again lately, I thought it might be nice to take a look at the opposite side:<br /> Where do splats benefit from another? How could a Werewolfpack be improved by including a Beast/Promethean/Sin-Eater?<br /> What does a Mage stand to gain in cooperating with a Vampire? Etc. Etc.<br /> Some likely scenarios for interaction and cooperation?<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, imo Vampires most obviously benefit by having someone of equal standing take care of the business during daylight hours. In exchange, one of the most unique abilities of Kindred is the Blood bond. Having access to a tool like that is very effective in e.g. creating a mole that usual methods of detection would probably not pick up. Their tendency to create extensive human networks they influence has quite some value in and off itself, and the usefulness of Majesty or Obfuscate for about any Splat cannot be denied.<br /> <br /> Werewolves bring a lot to the table, especially in regards to direct physical combat, but access to the hisil is not to be underestimated. I could see a Changling join a pack and fill the spot of e.g. an Irraka, offering access to a whole new world of possible prey in the Hedge as well as unorthodox abilities, which help in taking their prey by surprise.<br /> <br /> Mages might benefit from having a combat/stealth specced Beast with them: not only could this catch the target off-guard, a Beast is able and likely to use abilities where a Mage is at a disadvantage (in the middle of a crowded street for example). Not to meantion easy access to other Realms without having to have all the necessary Arcana (no Mastigos/Mind in the Team, but want to go to the Temenos? Fret not!).<br /> <br /> Prometheans would be happy to team up with anyone that kind of understands their plight and sympathizes, and some actively study other supernaturals, so there's that.<br /> <br /> Demons are likely to make use of just about anything to fumble with GM Infrastructure, and Beasts might be especially useful for that, being as detached from the GM as they come.<br /> <br /> <br /> Likely scenarios? Ordo Dracul Mekhet looking to widen his horizon, a Beast looking for Kinship, an Ulgan looking to study supernaturals, the Elodoth remnant of pack stumbling upon one another. Each would have something to gain from an alliance, but also take on considerable risks, and it would be not without some hardships that they would have to overcome their initial distrust. But it could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T15:42:12-07:00","id":1136407,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters have a power that allows them to disguise the cause of death of a body for any forensic analysis. It gets out that one of them can do this and she'll be on the speed-dial every supernatural in the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T17:26:12-07:00","id":1136453,"title":"","content":"Werewolves can potentially have anything as packmates, depending on how willing they are to deal with xenophobia and ruthless Oath interpretations. Blood bound spirits doing our bidding for their fix as the vampire regains Vitae by drinking from a packmate, which they'd heal in a matter of minutes? Sounds legit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T17:30:14-07:00","id":1136455,"title":"","content":"It might seem munchkiny. But i wonder you if you can stack things like pack benefits with krewe, motley pledge, etc. So that everyone in the group, regardless of splat, gets the benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T17:54:21-07:00","id":1136466,"title":"","content":"I have to imagine you can, it's not as if you take a pledge and it cancels out your pack advantage. I suppose the more pertinent question would be if krewes and motleys allow for werewolves and other supernaturals the way a pack does.<br /> <br /> And regarding werewolves, obviously a mage, changeling or sin-eater would be useful in opening gateways to other places so werewolves could get to otherwise hard-to-reach prey. Werewolves can steal secrets from the bones of the dead, as well, which would make them useful to folks who might need that, like maybe vampires and mages. Werewolf packs can mesh well with Circle of the Crone covens and give them some extra back-up in their tensions with the Lancea et Sanctum, though it's entirely possible you would have werewolves bent more towards the LS doctrine.<br /> <br /> Hunters could learn a lot about the hunt from werewolves, and the werewolves could learn a lot about mortal supernatural-hunter tactics in exchange. As well as the forces behind cells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T10:47:15-07:00","id":1136634,"title":"","content":"Beasts are pretty well equipped for cooperation, by design. With the right Atavism they're second only to Werewolves in terms of how easily they can provide an unlimited blood supply for Vampires. Changelings have powerful enemies, so the appeal of a powerful ally who is immune to their usual weaknesses is pretty obvious. Being immune to Disquiet makes them very nearly the only reliable friends a Promethean will ever make outside their own kind. And just about everybody can benefit from the ease with which the Begotten open doors to other worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T14:28:34-07:00","id":1136716,"title":"","content":"I concur. Also, don't forget that Mother's Kiss helps especially weaker kin, and Beasts are certain to welcome the additional Satiety income via Family Dinner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T15:03:24-07:00","id":1136723,"title":"","content":"Mages have a lot to gain from being good friends with a crew of influential vampires. Bloodsuckers tend to accrue all kinds of social resources, cash, property and such, that many Mages either shun through lack of interest or avoid for fear of drawing the attention of the Seers. Mages have a wide variety of types of mystical sites they desire regular, safe access to in the form of Verges, Hallows, Loci and Mysteries. Influential vampires could be the means by which a Cabal gets access to them, by bribing/influencing local council officials, leasing properties through chains of shell companies (to better hide the Pentacles movements from Seers) or just through loaning substantial cash sums. <br /> <br /> A vampire also has himself to offer, as a test subject. I can imagine many Mages might relish the opportunity to work out exactly how the Vampiric Curse works and will offer mystical boons in return. A willing active assistant is likely to be a lot more informative that a prisoner after all.<br /> <br /> On the return end, the Mages could offer a Coterie allies who can deal with all manner of threats vampires might even have trouble detecting. Poltergeist activity ruining the vibe in your favourite feeding grounds? Your friendly neighbourhood Moros can sort that. The Strix infiltrating the Prince's Court? Perhaps a Thrysus could sort out who's who? The gift of short term spells, or Imbued trinkets, would also be powerful bargaining chips, if not the sort that I can see many Mages wanting to give out too often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T15:18:23-07:00","id":1136731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1136376-cooperation-of-various-splats?p=1136723#post1136723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages have a lot to gain from being good friends with a crew of influential vampires. Bloodsuckers tend to accrue all kinds of social resources, cash, property and such, that many Mages either shun through lack of interest or avoid for fear of drawing the attention of the Seers. Mages have a wide variety of types of mystical sites they desire regular, safe access to in the form of Verges, Hallows, Loci and Mysteries. Influential vampires could be the means by which a Cabal gets access to them, by bribing/influencing local council officials, leasing properties through chains of shell companies (to better hide the Pentacles movements from Seers) or just through loaning substantial cash sums. <br /> <br /> A vampire also has himself to offer, as a test subject. I can imagine many Mages might relish the opportunity to work out exactly how the Vampiric Curse works and will offer mystical boons in return. A willing active assistant is likely to be a lot more informative that a prisoner after all.<br /> <br /> On the return end, the Mages could offer a Coterie allies who can deal with all manner of threats vampires might even have trouble detecting. Poltergeist activity ruining the vibe in your favourite feeding grounds? Your friendly neighbourhood Moros can sort that. The Strix infiltrating the Prince's Court? Perhaps a Thrysus could sort out who's who? The gift of short term spells, or Imbued trinkets, would also be powerful bargaining chips, if not the sort that I can see many Mages wanting to give out too often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as Mind &quot;Avoid the Day-Sleep&quot; and Forces &quot;Redirect sunlight around me&quot; protective items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T15:26:25-07:00","id":1136735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1136376-cooperation-of-various-splats?p=1136731#post1136731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Such as Mind &quot;Avoid the Day-Sleep&quot; and Forces &quot;Redirect sunlight around me&quot; protective items.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would leave it very much up to the ST as to whether Supernal Magic could so casually counter the negative aspects of Vampirism, I mean, if the games primarily a V:TR affair and the Mages are NPCs it risks totally undermining some core themes of the game. On the other hand if its a Mage game and the Vampires are the NPC's it might make an interesting experiment, with potentially disastrous consequences for the Cabal when vamps from across the country start battering down their door looking for the miracle cure, and no way could one Cabal create enough Supply to meet that Demand. Either way, I am sure the Mages could concoct a host of devices and spells that the Vamps would find useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T16:57:33-07:00","id":1136757,"title":"","content":"That's a nice plothook!<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul and Mysterium would probably go along well.<br /> <br /> There is one more benefit for werewolves I forgot: you have silver-resistant packmates. This is especially important if you face savy enemies who know about this and are bend on making use of that - only to find that the Loupe-Garou-Horrored Beast does not care much about silver, and proceeds to punch them in the face, possible with lethal force. The Gangrel merely laughs at the 'deadly' stab wound and slits their throat. Might not decide the fight, but certainly can turn the momentum.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T18:31:24-07:00","id":1136777,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, if you're fighting werewolves, a silver based Metalflesh Changeling is your new best friend","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T19:32:46-07:00","id":1136798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1136376-cooperation-of-various-splats?p=1136757#post1136757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a nice plothook!<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul and Mysterium would probably go along well.<br /> <br /> There is one more benefit for werewolves I forgot: you have silver-resistant packmates. This is especially important if you face savy enemies who know about this and are bend on making use of that - only to find that the Loupe-Garou-Horrored Beast does not care much about silver, and proceeds to punch them in the face, possible with lethal force. The Gangrel merely laughs at the 'deadly' stab wound and slits their throat. Might not decide the fight, but certainly can turn the momentum.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Silver-only Matter repulsion spells, for all your argentum-allergic furry friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T19:38:33-07:00","id":1136799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1136376-cooperation-of-various-splats?p=1136735#post1136735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would leave it very much up to the ST as to whether Supernal Magic could so casually counter the negative aspects of Vampirism, I mean, if the games primarily a V:TR affair and the Mages are NPCs it risks totally undermining some core themes of the game. On the other hand if its a Mage game and the Vampires are the NPC's it might make an interesting experiment, with potentially disastrous consequences for the Cabal when vamps from across the country start battering down their door looking for the miracle cure, and no way could one Cabal create enough Supply to meet that Demand. Either way, I am sure the Mages could concoct a host of devices and spells that the Vamps would find useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, bear in mind that it is Dissonance vulnerable Supernal magic. And an oddly shadowed person is obviously supernatural.<br /> <br /> You could use more Forces to create a hologram of the vampire over their sunlight-cloak... but that is tricky as well. And stops Dominate (since targets can't see the Vampire's eyes, just the hologram).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T21:33:48-07:00","id":1136822,"title":"","content":"In my first Werewolf chronicle the pack had a murder spirit causing bad resonance in their territory. Now they could kill it, though it wasn't easy, but it would just reform in the deep Shadow and then return at its appointed time. The pack finally dealt with it by gaining the aid of a Mage who used Spirit magic to drain off the spirit's essence during the fight so that this time when the pack killed it, with no essence remaining the spirit stayed dead.<br /> \u200bThe Mage later called in the favor owed. He was trying to investigate a disturbance that was spreading outwards from a wound in the shadow, but couldn't go very deep in because the riled up Spirits kept driving him back. That is where a group of savage wolves designed from the ground up to hunt within the shadow proved useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T13:54:46-07:00","id":1137023,"title":"","content":"So, Mummies and Demons.<br /> <br /> Unchained offer the Arisen perfect recall (as long as they can be trusted), excellent information gathering abilities (if not quite up to Mage talents), and a ready source of non-Relic items of power.<br /> <br /> Mummies offer a Cult to hide amongst (and potentially make Pacts with), and a potent ally to beat Hunter Angels off their trail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T14:12:43-07:00","id":1137030,"title":"","content":"Demons tend to avoid cults, since they're easily manipulated by the God-Machine. Though throughout the books we see that cults aren't so much a Mummy-only thing, revolving around vampires, werewolves, mages, spirits, even ghosts and others. They're just starting to get mechanical support for it now.<br /> <br /> Providing they could trust each other, however, a Demon's ability to download and potentially store memories or spy on enemies through multiple identities would be pretty valuable for mummies.<br /> <br /> The Demon Storytellers Guide has a really excellently handled and very informative 'how they feel about others' section for Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-03-2017, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:15:32-07:00","id":1137061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1136376-cooperation-of-various-splats?p=1136735#post1136735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would leave it very much up to the ST as to whether Supernal Magic could so casually counter the negative aspects of Vampirism, I mean, if the games primarily a V:TR affair and the Mages are NPCs it risks totally undermining some core themes of the game. On the other hand if its a Mage game and the Vampires are the NPC's it might make an interesting experiment, with potentially disastrous consequences for the Cabal when vamps from across the country start battering down their door looking for the miracle cure, and no way could one Cabal create enough Supply to meet that Demand. Either way, I am sure the Mages could concoct a host of devices and spells that the Vamps would find useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would totally allow a mage to shield a vampire from sunlight. I'd also have it inflict blindness upon them, as the light would be unable to reach their eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:28:40-07:00","id":1137067,"title":"","content":"I know this is less of a combat example, but our Mastigos in a crossover game buffed my characters social abilities when I was doing Elysium stuff.<br /> <br /> I helped him against a time mage by using Dominate to tell the mage not to use magic.<br /> <br /> I tossed a Rahu against a vampire in a death match that had the stated rules of &quot;No using Disciplines.&quot; (I felt very cheeky with that one.)<br /> <br /> I crashed my character's car into a raging Rahu because my character was a vampire with resilience.<br /> <br /> I also drove said car into the domain of a God so our mage could fight said god. (He would have had issues getting there because the God had a servant that nearly killed the Rahu, and said servant had minor teleportation powers.)<br /> <br /> My character was getting tortured by an Elder, so our werewolf friends busted in to save me.<br /> <br /> Our characters had issues with the police and arrest warrants, so I used my character's connections to see those go away.<br /> <br /> I also negotiated a deal with a Forsaken Pack to leave our territory alone; the pack didn't respect our werewolves, but I was playing an Invictus Ventrue and I touched upon the Alpha's sense of honor.<br /> <br /> That's some of the highlights from our game. I can post some more stuff, if you guys would like to hear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:09:51-07:00","id":1137096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1136376-cooperation-of-various-splats?p=1137061#post1137061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would totally allow a mage to shield a vampire from sunlight. I'd also have it inflict blindness upon them, as the light would be unable to reach their eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not really how Shielding works in Mage. It's not limited or constrained by science.<br /> <br /> A mage doesn't direct the light bypass the vampire, rather it protects the vampire from the essence of the light.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, even though the spell would be a minor Forces 2 effect, the social and political implications of actually employing the spell would be potentially catastrophic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T18:46:22-07:00","id":1137151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1136376-cooperation-of-various-splats?p=1137096#post1137096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's not really how Shielding works in Mage. It's not limited or constrained by science.<br /> <br /> A mage doesn't direct the light bypass the vampire, rather it protects the vampire from the essence of the light.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, even though the spell would be a minor Forces 2 effect, the social and political implications of actually employing the spell would be potentially catastrophic.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies. I guess that shows how much I've run Mage. I'd been imagining the spell preventing the sunlight from touching the vampire rather than just making the vampire immune to the ill effects of sunlight. I'd be a lot less likely to let that work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T19:02:54-07:00","id":1137157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1136376-cooperation-of-various-splats?p=1137151#post1137151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My apologies. I guess that shows how much I've run Mage. I'd been imagining the spell preventing the sunlight from touching the vampire rather than just making the vampire immune to the ill effects of sunlight. I'd be a lot less likely to let that work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A mage CAN cast a spell to redirect the light, but Shielding protects against the effects of the light.<br /> <br /> However, I would let the mage employ the spell because it was so unbalancing and with potentially immeasurable social and political repercussions. That's just the type of Hubris and shortsightedness that characterizes mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T22:01:01-07:00","id":1137193,"title":"","content":"A Werewolf is facing off against a spirit that has claimed one of his loved ones, the spirit is mocking him, taunting him with the knowledge that in order to stop the spirit he will have to kill the person he loves. In steps a Mage who uses Spirit to expel the spirit into the waiting jaws of the Werewolf, then uses Life to undue any changes the spirit's presence made to the victim.<br /> <br /> \u200bVampires are vulnerable during their day sleep, so he shares his haven with a pack of trusted Werewolves, security is no longer much of an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T00:54:33-07:00","id":1137229,"title":"","content":"In a much more mundane act of cooperation, when a vampire in my game was working to become the ambassador between Kindred and Uratha, she ended up letting a pack of werewolves work at her feeding ground, a run down bar. They spiced it up a bit, allowing more of a variety of prey, and used their jobs as cover for their piracy, as they were sea-hunters. They also had no problem getting rid of anyone who had seen something they shouldn't have seen.<br /> <br /> The werewolves didn't like the previous ambassador, who was apparently too uppity for them. Since vampire PC had said she was more willing to be fair with them in the ambassadors place,, they made the position open in the first place by killing the existing ambassador.<br /> <br /> In my changeling game, there was a vampire. I didn't run it so I don't recall the specifics, but I believe he had lost his faith and made a pact with another changeling to get it back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-04-2017, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}